le":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c81fecac446addd66339f4f9450fe59514c5344e91bdd68299e138304bfbbd1c","compact":"b441be2c73933932f7d1e6aa2bf5545e7dcb5e8f29c0ce46213e155b4cfc7da0","nasal":"0f5e460021c8a2a7462565e7af4fe749b0feec8586ca08b0820e5af58ee3eb82"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-5","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":5,"english":"As if swallowing up the welkin and touching the lord of stars, abolishing the sky decorated with stars and the solar disc, and cleaving the clouds, the unfatigued Hanuman began to cross over that sea.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.406,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055005","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4d44ae2d2285c5e083083e7cb8b857fe03be4344bd4eb750e13a082c1bed6ce7","compact":"7b6d511213f6f87d653571889aa1c4ab98f31891f45b018de3589ca19175ba77","nasal":"09c45956629f6404cc0385484431b281ac6f97fc54c718b3f829e378192f099c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-6","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":6,"english":"And (on all sides) mighty masses of clouds, sable, crimson, blue, Manjistha-hued, and greenred, looked exceedingly beautiful.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"804d4ec206b0f6b099f3a8ddbd58bbd4941b3c675c378afeb3f1a0ca75c17708","compact":"43aa51a3e1970625bfe91f4d7acb54a0b1bb7757cc783e838257d29298d8541d","nasal":"333758a19dd8ffdb1956ca37259c7d28399bdd00a9f4b505dfdef167a268d203"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":7,"english":"And now entering into clouds and now imerging from them, he, again and again becoming visible and lost to sight, looked like the Moon.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.571,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d99d29b8fb179900d020fc0e1649851940e034a1bf9201ef14c2c2aff2923d21","compact":"55dbacb51f6362dd27de3e6d4f955c4a89b6548975ec07f238a283bc64f60f4d","nasal":"8e3e1bda19167a50f6180c2339c3ea546c26e30b220f7b5c7d167446a0e68df5"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":8,"english":"And sending up mighty sounds, that exceedingly energetic one gifted with a powerful voice like that of the clouds, having slain the foremost Rākşasas and rendered his name famous, having filled the city with lamentations and afflicted Rāvana, having distressed the mighty heroes and paid obeisance to Vaidehī, again held his course along the mid-ocean.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.863,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2eb672e4181d83bffdb6219912523f7a4e521740725a7f81913c865e75ed0a6d","compact":"731940ae0418934849b131d8e025465efdd0d02b62859b553db9f13d8ac226d4","nasal":"e2364507bb5047d10532df72b7f34a5306cbe884247a3f9c5f4f199d5dcf2226"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":9,"english":"And touching Mainaka-foremost of mountains-that one endowed with prowess proceeded amain like an iron dart let go from a string.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.846,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0bf35cb706e6fe72892878f3c7440e8c7c26290b3911281de7a3385b0dec3148","compact":"904d763f2a3860e6392efe0eeaddd218e9d5020f73c85f67e7e6d0238c3d0cf2","nasal":"e897226e83aee7cef6642cd496d778f5417704b1bda0f795910d635fa8bb1286"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":10,"english":"And from a distance approaching and beholding that mighty mountain, Mahendra, resembling clouds, that redoubted monkey began to roar.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.661,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cfa797cf5ec4c4d71f8f47ecfe44425727b08720d65f91e8d83d09a9e1b01fdb","compact":"7326c689541ab7894c628b4ea61a7a117e27e85fe4859906c71e6a7441eb10e7","nasal":"674b6ab362b0e274d60f1e053ee237d155a4548fc284b736a8ea026f50f36440"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":11,"english":"Hearing those sounds as he kept crying, those monkeys (sitting) around, eager to see their friend, became extremely anxious.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"faedd852129d1e1808608aeea3ab6953735ca44c99f1d5bcc7ca2194a956561f","compact":"6159b96ebfe0fb9f8abf7c29824efce3588d1cd30b8d6524abd457dea0dcdef1","nasal":"653fff823b1ad53411c58d676dd424ecb4c7398737ee4c6436512f6133dde8a4"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":12,"english":"And that best of monkeys, Jambavan, with a joyful heart addressing all the monkeys, said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9d505da6b61f0f99266b9e384f94def844e28ba762994f2091e7288bc08a336d","compact":"42b8e18ed10d97166d1dd70e1afab5dd02cefbd9b3107f881596c0222ddcd7fb","nasal":"b3282507bedaa077c41e51b9a06f8892c440944e6ecf7c6eb8c28c2b6bf579e9"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":13,"english":"Hanumān has succeeded completely. There is no doubt about this. If he were unsuccessful, he would not utter shouts as these.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0e2414cc569bb326b91f953c2bee2b4a4bf30207bea4c277027c3ee3b9542b0a","compact":"33ea1d20067fac1fb79de3396cddaefb0d068e95caae06db37fda8da54a767ee","nasal":"f6d6ed508f804a91ea0bcc2f9e71c95d77f6cad1cf2ff3973eb1169cfe9babea"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":14,"english":"And hearing the sounds produced by the violent movements of the arms of that highsouled (hero), as well as the shouts of that magnanimous one, the monkeys, filled with delight, leapt up on all sides.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.763,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055014","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f92d10e26843b6681513e5eb0854037fb25721021f2faa63cdf9c0dfbbf99da0","compact":"05ec8983dcb75940eda7911ac1fcf33ea7df33960e491d1a4525edea27c56e3d","nasal":"05ec8983dcb75940eda7911ac1fcf33ea7df33960e491d1a4525edea27c56e3d"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-15","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":15,"english":"And they, eager to have a sight of Hanumān, joyfully went from mountain-top to mountaintop and from peak on to peak.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.891,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055015","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f79dd5d448f815fc5bbee984a701fc3ace42a3e4dbe7bbe82a36f3e3715da235","compact":"23aa800e434ce1e690cc495cae32d1f799985633ca47ea0c6a7df6f1af17bbeb","nasal":"2e5b1ed76ce05e2b8377cee4185d54a4ad567b6c9fecfb6fa31b89a6fba326d9"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-16","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":16,"english":"And influenced by joy, the monkeys remained holding a bough at the top of a tree, and waving their clean apparels.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.647,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055016","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6e2fd3ba2d84dfcf7c981215ad227bd9e7ee22ebb1cccd1ff408a2062808bfd5","compact":"2b7a2ec51a811877aa8b3c73b319b918a25a2c3852b0a8f1335ce2040c8154dd","nasal":"6fbd965898e8d1b993d5d84c84d608282e0f40e130ef6102fdc0350e420985e6"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-17","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":17,"english":"And seeing that mighty monkey resembling a mass of clouds, alighting, those monkeys stood joining their hands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055017","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5a5b8286487568f5f1eca9fb55156f4232fca30664afec9c013c89cbfcea0a2a","compact":"b9682e73b1bd45293f98eb5c91a4d949497a07da4644227d4ef3cfdae8a79cc7","nasal":"644e3b8d482867fab6e49c4394af1c82267949c8fa6fbe339fe3c87f2be175dc"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-18","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":18,"english":"Then the vehement monkey resembling a hill, having leapt up from that mountain, alighted on the top of that (other) mountain (Mahendra) filled with trees.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.4,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055018","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9fdb9d23667b8f8101dbbb130f25b827d903305530d8f29c4004a25f1da61cf9","compact":"1eec591a142ebbf5c3d119df749c58d102db45e3dc0b2e01b41e9d446b5b727a","nasal":"8e0e740df7da327fb74cf4229095dc1feeca624fc76e215b82e3cecad071af26"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-19","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":19,"english":"Then with joyful hearts, all the principal monkeys stood encircling the high-souled Hanuman.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055019","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"12f40dad9060433ecb5bffac2c6f2f48770192d146696798a8c06949571a4fec","compact":"dd60561a209b01d2ca452a3331864956377f2c123d6c39f9671e601f5d65fb2c","nasal":"f6c3e5e95b0d8a685a14af6eba8831dea8052d719afaad3b4b86d0a8723f4433"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-20","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":20,"english":"And surrounding him, they experienced excess of delight, and drew near the newcomer with joyful faces. And bringing fruits and roots, the monkeys honoured that chief of monkeys, the offspring of the Wind-god.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.81,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055020","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2b1efb259165984babf87fd5c6ff8a419457a112a5c81dd0331c294ac2564961","compact":"713d0df49da2c406b0a4efe49889dca8929030ab26b2d464ea04fb2631adf637","nasal":"713d0df49da2c406b0a4efe49889dca8929030ab26b2d464ea04fb2631adf637"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-21","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":21,"english":"And surrounding him, they experienced excess of delight, and drew near the newcomer with joyful faces. And bringing fruits and roots, the monkeys honoured that chief of monkeys, the offspring of the Wind-god.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055021","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9a2278ca6a9bb48d83f0b11022183bee96156cd34323e6c277f31651ce4b839e","compact":"9b86a2573ebab060b50f1373d9a89d96dfd1e271794c991bac81db98af23407c","nasal":"9b86a2573ebab060b50f1373d9a89d96dfd1e271794c991bac81db98af23407c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-22","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":22,"english":"And some, filled with delight, sent shouts, and some raised ululations; and the foremost monkeys fetched branches of trees. (To serve for a seat for Hanuman)","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.544,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055022","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"64db2ff5a93aa6f6e62da4fc4c65f593fbafe4fc72cac2c1d2251052fa5a33bb","compact":"cbfa34cc65d5e184b0cf739504d15b8422c4a3c10be3d0d8a4d5907ccad99cd6","nasal":"cbfa34cc65d5e184b0cf739504d15b8422c4a3c10be3d0d8a4d5907ccad99cd6"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-55-23","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":55,"verse":23,"english":"And that mighty monkey, Hanumān, saluted his superiors an the aged, headed by Jāmbavan, as well as Prince Angada.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-57-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5055023","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cd18a33b0a5bb7b03ba13e08ec2e859308571d1fc5a6789ff81c997b0f2c4d44","compact":"61f7b554f16ab91878c0c816f0e1b0ec7b2c9c465ecdd684a945b9330500ce11","nasal":"847a6ba33